From: unjordi <jordi@ciencias.unam.mx>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: wake on charger attach/detach

With the battmgr supplies registered without a wakeup source, routine
battery telemetry no longer wakes the AP -- but a charger attach or
detach must still wake it long enough to service the charge-start
handshake before it re-suspends. On QCS8550/kalama-class parts the
charger is handled entirely in the ADSP and the AP has no dedicated
charger IRQ; the only wake path is the glink doorbell, and ucsi_glink in
this tree carries no wakeup logic of its own, so the battmgr client must
provide it.

Mark the battmgr device wakeup-capable and, in the notification handler,
arm a short hard wakeup event only on the charger/connector notification
class -- NOTIF_USB_PROPERTY (0x32) and NOTIF_WLS_PROPERTY (0x34) -- and
never on NOTIF_BAT_PROPERTY (0x30), which is the high-rate telemetry that
constitutes the storm. This mirrors the client-side wakeup pattern that
upstream adopted for ucsi_glink (device_init_wakeup() + a bounded
pm_wakeup event on the connector event), applied to the battmgr client.

The USB/WLS notification class fires on plug/unplug and PD contract
changes, which are infrequent, so this wakes on a real charger event
without re-introducing the telemetry storm. A finer filter (waking only
when usb.online actually toggles) is possible but needs cached online
state; the notification-class scoping already excludes the telemetry
that caused the storm.

Signed-off-by: unjordi <jordi@ciencias.unam.mx>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 #include <linux/mutex.h>
 #include <linux/nvmem-consumer.h>
 #include <linux/of_device.h>
+#include <linux/pm_wakeup.h>
 #include <linux/power_supply.h>
 #include <linux/property.h>
 #include <linux/soc/qcom/pdr.h>
@@ -34,6 +35,13 @@ enum qcom_battmgr_variant {
 #define NOTIF_BAT_PROPERTY		0x30
 #define NOTIF_USB_PROPERTY		0x32
 #define NOTIF_WLS_PROPERTY		0x34
+
+/*
+ * Hold a wakeup source briefly across a charger attach/detach so the AP
+ * stays up long enough to service the charge-start handshake before it
+ * re-enters suspend.
+ */
+#define QCOM_BATTMGR_WAKEUP_MS		50
 #define NOTIF_BAT_STATUS		0x80
 #define NOTIF_BAT_INFO			0x81
 #define NOTIF_BAT_CHARGING_STATE	0x83
@@ -1214,9 +1222,11 @@ static void qcom_battmgr_notification(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr,
 		power_supply_changed(battmgr->bat_psy);
 		break;
 	case NOTIF_USB_PROPERTY:
+		pm_wakeup_dev_event(battmgr->dev, QCOM_BATTMGR_WAKEUP_MS, true);
 		power_supply_changed(battmgr->usb_psy);
 		break;
 	case NOTIF_WLS_PROPERTY:
+		pm_wakeup_dev_event(battmgr->dev, QCOM_BATTMGR_WAKEUP_MS, true);
 		power_supply_changed(battmgr->wls_psy);
 		break;
 	default:
@@ -1737,6 +1747,13 @@ static int qcom_battmgr_probe(struct auxiliary_device *adev,
 					     "failed to register wireless charing power supply\n");
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Wake the AP on a charger attach/detach (the USB/WLS notifications
+	 * handled above); the routine battery telemetry is left to the
+	 * supplies, which are registered without a wakeup source.
+	 */
+	device_init_wakeup(dev, true);
+
 	battmgr->client = devm_pmic_glink_client_alloc(dev, PMIC_GLINK_OWNER_BATTMGR,
 						       qcom_battmgr_callback,
 						       qcom_battmgr_pdr_notify,
